.TH PSMatrixZeros 3 2023-12-09 "PsyC 0.9.3" "PsyC Library Functions Manual"

.SH NAME
\fBPSMatrixZeros\fR \- Create a new zero\-filled matrix

.SH LIBRARY
PsyC (-lpsyc)

.SH SYNOPSIS

.B
#include <psyc/maths.h>

.I
PSMatrix  
.br
\fBPSMatrixZeros\fR(\fIint ndims\fR, \fI...\fR)
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create a new, zero-filled, matrix having number of dimensions defined by \fIndims\fR. The shape of the matrix is given by variadic arguments that follows \fIndims\fR.
.br
If the matrix cannot be allocated, \fIerrno\fR will be set to \fIENOMEM\fR.  

.SH RETURN VALUES
The allocated matrix or \fINULL\fR if:

.RS 4
\[bu] the number of dimensions (\fIndims\fR) is greater than \fIPS_MATRIX_MAX_DIMENSIONS\fR or less than one.
.br

\[bu] it's not possible to allocate the matrix in memory.
.RE
.RE

.br
\fBWARN\fR:  the address pointed by the returned pointer should never be freed directly. The specific function \fIPSMatrixFree\fR should be used instead.
.br

.SH SEE ALSO
psyc(1)
